Since this is really an issue of the PEPS package (and where it might run), 
I am taking this topic to where it belongs, to the  pepswin group.   Most 
of you are already members of both groups.  If necessary, post or e-mail me 
for add to that group,  etc.  I am posting about some new things there, 
perhaps later today.

cjl

The only specific interaction between PEPS and P?S/8 (and also OS/8) is the 
specifics of support for DECtape.  Thanks to a couple of minor patches to 
pdp8.exe (the SIMH executable) DECtapes can be any length up to 4K blocks.  
Originally this was intended to have support of real-world extra-long 
DECtapes of 3300 blocks, but there are also useful features to be gained 
supporting the "fantasy" size as well.  Also, specifically for the benefit 
of prior releases of P?S/8 (primarily, there is perhaps a modicum of this 
pertinent to the latest release) SIMH can permanently place the device 66 
LPT off-line.  As such, there are two different ways to launch P?S/8 for 
any particular version, etc.  Like PDP-12 DIAL-MS, P?S/8 LPT: support is by 
device discovery; failing to locate the hardware and the software reverts 
to the system console.  In Version 8Z (nearly) all utilities support the /T 
command-line switch to prevent the detection.  Future releases may reverse 
the polarity of the switch to instead enable printer output, but 
regardless, the newer releases exert some control over the issue whereas 
the older releases did not (PEPS has provisional support for an old Version 
8T system which has no program support to disable the LPT: As such, it is 
mandatory for that older system, but needed less and less with newer 
releases.  Future releases will reduce this to near zero; however, for the 
present, PEPS will have the duality regarding the printer, etc.


