>>>
>>> So, for the present, we have a "virtual" extended-length file on each of 
>>> up to 8 logical devices.
>>>
>>> The OS8CON system program can convert OS/8 text files and P?S/8 text 
>>> files in both conversion directions.  There is also support for 
>>> extended-length output files cognizant of the restriction as shown above.  
>>> The notion of extended-length files is undergoing revision for the next 
>>> release; at that point, the restrictions will cease to exist and be 
>>> bullet-proof.
>>>
>>> If a string of TFS files gets too "bunched up" because of many editing 
>>> sessions, use OS8CON to output to a scratch file [the default is to what 
>>> OS/8 would use as the first file on an otherwise zeroed-out DTA1:, then use 
>>> OS8CON to bring the files back with the sizes restandardized..Please note 
>>> that the more into the description, the more far-fetched the problem is, 
>>> but there is always an ultimate answer.
>>>
>>> Lastly, if you use PEPS, edit the files in the host environment with 
>>> your choice of editor.  Thus, there is no longer a dependency on OS/8.  But 
>>> in the package, you get both and you can use both systems "the best of both 
>>> worlds" etc.
